{
 "description": "Shared by plugin/src/verdict/aggregate.js and host/vaultd/judge.py. Samples are the raw model answers {decision, max_minutes, reason, parseFailed?}; requested and ceiling come from vaultd's request.create answer. expected is hand-derived from the rule, not generated by either implementation.",
 "rule": [
  "A sample is normalised first: an unknown decision is c; an approval (a|b) whose max_minutes is not an integer from 1 to 480 is c; max_minutes of other samples is irrelevant; a sample with parseFailed: true is c whatever else it says.",
  "No samples: c.",
  "All samples d: d (the agent is locked), minutes 0.",
  "Not all samples a|b (any other mix of c/d/a/b, parse failures included): c, minutes 0, no lock.",
  "All samples a|b: decision a if any sample is a, else b; minutes = min(every sample's max_minutes, requested, ceiling.maxMinutes), and also min narrowMinutes when the decision is a (narrowMinutes defaults to 30 when absent; the vectors always give it). Non-integer or missing requested/maxMinutes count as 0.",
  "minutes below 1: c, minutes 0, no lock."
 ],
 "version": 1,
